# Deploy user's crontab — backup/DR schedule (config-as-code; see
# docs/runbooks/database-backup-restore.md, bring-up checklist step 8).
#
# This file is the canonical source: a rebuilt droplet gets its schedule
# from the repo, not from a human's memory of a runbook. Install/replace
# as the deploy user with:
#
#   crontab deploy/cron.d/priori-backups.cron
#
# WARNING: `crontab <file>` replaces the user's ENTIRE crontab. If the
# deploy user ever carries unrelated entries, merge them into this file
# (in the repo, via MR) instead of hand-editing on the droplet — hand
# edits are exactly the drift this file exists to prevent.

# nightly DB dump + uploads tar, age-encrypted, copied offsite
# (after the 00:15 UTC nightly transitions; before nothing that matters)
15 1 * * * RCLONE_REMOTE=spaces:priori-crm-backups /srv/priori/bin/db_backup.sh >> /srv/priori/backups/backup.log 2>&1

# hourly uploads mirror to the bucket (freshness tier; heartbeat for the
# dead-man's switch). The mirror goes THROUGH the crypt remote (client-side
# encryption, #82); the plain remote is used only for the heartbeat.
5 * * * * BACKUP_BUCKET_REMOTE=spaces:priori-crm-backups UPLOADS_CRYPT_REMOTE=spaces-crypt-uploads: /srv/priori/bin/uploads_sync.sh >> /srv/priori/backups/uploads-sync.log 2>&1
